  <!-- 05 — KEY DESIGN DECISIONS -->
  <div class="case-shell" id="decisions">
    <section class="case-section">
      <p class="sec-label">5. Key design decisions</p>
      <h2 class="case-heading">Data clarity through restraint.</h2>

      <!-- Decision 01 -->
      <div class="decision-article">
        <div>
          <h3 class="decision-title">1. Surface renewals before they happen.</h3>
          <p class="decision-body">
            A dedicated section at the top of the dashboard surfaces renewals
            within the next 7 days — directly addressing the most common pain
            point: renewal surprises.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="compare-pair">
          <div class="compare-card compare-card--before">
            <p class="compare-label">The problem</p>
            <ul style="list-style:none;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.65rem;font-size:0.92rem;color:var(--muted);">
              <li>Charges appear after the fact</li>
              <li>No advance warning system</li>
              <li>Buried in calendar or bank app</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="compare-card compare-card--after">
            <p class="compare-label">The solution</p>
            <ul style="list-style:none;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.65rem;font-size:0.92rem;">
              <li>Renewals strip on dashboard</li>
              <li>7-day lookahead always visible</li>
              <li>Push notification reminders</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Decision 02 -->
      <div class="decision-article">
        <div>
          <h3 class="decision-title">2. Category system that links list to analytics.</h3>
          <p class="decision-body">
            Each subscription gets a category — Entertainment, Productivity, Health,
            Storage — with a distinct colour token. The colour runs as a left border
            on each list row and fills the analytics chart, creating a visual link
            without overloading the interface.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="compare-card compare-card--before" style="border-style:solid;">
            <p class="compare-label">Category colours</p>
            <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.6rem;margin-top:0.5rem;">
              <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.75rem;">
                <div style="width:3px;height:2rem;background:#e74c3c;border-radius:2px;flex-shrink:0;"></div>
                <span style="font-size:0.88rem;">Entertainment</span>
              </div>
              <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.75rem;">
                <div style="width:3px;height:2rem;background:#1abc9c;border-radius:2px;flex-shrink:0;"></div>
                <span style="font-size:0.88rem;">Productivity</span>
              </div>
              <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.75rem;">
                <div style="width:3px;height:2rem;background:#3498db;border-radius:2px;flex-shrink:0;"></div>
                <span style="font-size:0.88rem;">Health</span>
              </div>
              <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.75rem;">
                <div style="width:3px;height:2rem;background:#27ae60;border-radius:2px;flex-shrink:0;"></div>
                <span style="font-size:0.88rem;">Storage</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Decision 03 -->
      <div class="decision-article">
        <div>
          <h3 class="decision-title">3. Fast subscription setup — under 30 seconds.</h3>
          <p class="decision-body">
            A search-first entry field pulls from a library of 200+ common services
            with pre-filled logos and typical pricing, falling back to manual entry
            for anything unlisted.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="compare-pair">
            <div class="compare-card compare-card--before">
              <p class="compare-label">Manual entry (fallback)</p>
              <ul style="list-style:none;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.55rem;font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--muted);">
                <li>Service name</li>
                <li>Monthly amount</li>
                <li>Billing cycle</li>
                <li>Renewal date</li>
                <li>Category</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="compare-card compare-card--after">
              <p class="compare-label">Search-first entry</p>
              <ul style="list-style:none;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.55rem;font-size:0.88rem;">
                <li>Find service by name</li>
                <li>Logo + price pre-filled</li>
                <li>Set billing &amp; date</li>
                <li>Done in one step</li>
              </ul>
              <span class="compare-badge">~30 sec to add</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <!-- 06 — OUTCOMES -->
  <div class="case-shell" id="outcomes">
    <section class="case-section">
      <p class="sec-label">6. Prototype &amp; reflections</p>
      <h2 class="case-heading">28 screens. Every state accounted for.</h2>
      <p class="case-body-text" style="margin-top:1.5rem;max-width:580px;">
        The prototype covers all six main flows with realistic transitions and was
        designed to be self-navigable — a first-time viewer can explore without a guide.
      </p>

      <div class="outcomes-grid" style="margin-top:2.5rem;">
        <div class="outcomes-card outcomes-card--light">
          <p class="outcomes-card-label">Design outcomes</p>
          <ul class="outcomes-list">
            <li class="outcome-item">
              <span class="outcome-num">1.</span>
              <span>
                <span class="outcome-content-title">Renewals impossible to miss</span>
                <span class="outcome-content-body">Upcoming charges surface at the top of the dashboard, not buried in a calendar.</span>
              </span>
            </li>
            <li class="outcome-item">
              <span class="outcome-num">2.</span>
              <span>
                <span class="outcome-content-title">Monthly total always visible</span>
                <span class="outcome-content-body">A persistent summary bar keeps the cost visible while scrolling through the full list.</span>
              </span>
            </li>
            <li class="outcome-item">
              <span class="outcome-num">3.</span>
              <span>
                <span class="outcome-content-title">Edge cases revealed structural gaps</span>
                <span class="outcome-content-body">The interrupted onboarding scenario required rethinking subscription state persistence — improving the main flow too.</span>
              </span>
            </li>
            <li class="outcome-item">
              <span class="outcome-num">4.</span>
              <span>
                <span class="outcome-content-title">Data clarity requires restraint</span>
                <span class="outcome-content-body">The design process was largely one of removal — hiding data users don't need at that moment.</span>
              </span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="outcomes-card outcomes-card--violet">
          <p class="outcomes-card-label">What's next</p>
          <ul class="validation-list">
            <li class="validation-item">
              <p class="validation-title">Real-data testing</p>
              <p class="validation-note">Analytics views are based on assumed patterns. With real data, the most valuable chart might differ from what was designed.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="validation-item">
              <p class="validation-title">A/B test dashboard layout</p>
              <p class="validation-note">Testing subscription list vs analytics-first against actual engagement would be the first post-launch experiment.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="validation-item">
              <p class="validation-title">Bank integration</p>
              <p class="validation-note">Auto-detection from bank transaction data would dramatically reduce manual entry friction.</p>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

